
-------------------------------------------
BOSS 4.1 Release Note #  3   March 22, 1999
-------------------------------------------

(1)
For versions of BOSS 4.1 prior to today, please
note that the SASA components were mislabeled in the run summaries
(both sum file and ot file). I.e., for ethanol the columns below
for hydrophilic and hydrophobic should be reversed.

 SASA Analysis:
 Run    Tot. SASA      Volume      Hydrophilic    Hydrophobic    Aromatic
 20      215.001       279.765       159.280        55.721         0.000
  1      214.020       278.070       156.354        57.666         0.000
  2      214.736       279.426       156.271        58.465         0.000
...
 19      215.436       280.363       157.520        57.916         0.000

                                            Standard Deviations
           0.155         0.243         0.200         0.179         0.000

                                                 Averages
         214.989       279.721       157.845        57.144         0.000

The  breakdown earlier in the ot file was labeled correctly:

 Ave. Total Solute SASA   =    214.9894
 Ave. Total Solute Volume =    279.7212
 Hydrophobic SASA         =    157.8453
 Hydrophilic SASA         =     57.1441
 Aromatic    SASA         =      0.0000

The version of BOSS 4.1 (boss41m.tar.Z) that is now in the ftp site on omega has 
this problem corrected. 

(2)
One can now request the program to expand a Z-matrix that uses ranges (e.g. 0001-0022)
and AUTO commands into a full, explicit Z-matrix, which is output in
the sum file. One just uses the keyword FULL instead of NEWZMAT (or
NEWZM) in the par file. E.g.

replace
 Optimizer, ftol, simulated annealing parameters:
BFGS    0.000100NEWZM         0       0    0.0000    0.0000

with
 Optimizer, ftol, simulated annealing parameters:
BFGS    0.000100FULL          0       0    0.0000    0.0000


This is useful when (1) building a protein-ligand complex using pepz, which does not
recognize the range and AUTO designationsi, and (2) for generating a Z-matrix for
a flexible, custom solvent molecule when the original Z-matrix has AUTO designations
(AUTO designations are only valid for solute Z-matrices). 

